      "message": "Oh I see. Hmm, WDYT about splitting out like a `ValidateCanPresent` function and then calling it in `APIPresent` only then? (And we can have like an `ASSERT` in `Present`? \n\nI guess I\u0027m not too hard set on this, but I generally find the return value argument to be harder to follow and if we could avoid it, it would be nice.\n\nExample:\n```\nbool Surface::ValidateCanPresent() {\n    if (!mCurrentDevice) {\n        [[maybe_unused]] bool error \u003d mInstance-\u003eConsumedError(\n            DAWN_VALIDATION_ERROR(\"%s is not configured.\", this)\n        );\n        return false;\n    }\n    return true;\n}\n\nwgpu::Status Surface::APIPresent() {\n    if (!ValidateCanPresent()) {\n        return wgpu::Status::Error;\n    }\n    \n    // Other errors are handled as asynchronous errors and we return Success.\n    [[maybe_unused]] bool error \u003d GetCurrentDevice()-\u003eConsumedError(Present());\n    return wgpu::Status::Success;\n}\n\nMaybeError Surface::Present() {\n    DAWN_ASSERT(mCurrentDevice);\n    ...\n}\n```",
